// Title: GAC DLL Loaded Via Office Applications
// Sigma ID: 90217a70-13fc-48e4-b3db-0d836c5824ac
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Antonlovesdnb
// Date: 2020-02-19 | Modified: 2023-02-10
// ATT&CK: execution, T1204.002
// Description: Detects any GAC DLL being loaded by an Office Product
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate macro usage. Add the appropriate filter according to your environment
// References:
//   - https://medium.com/threatpunter/detecting-adversary-tradecraft-with-image-load-event-logging-and-eql-8de93338c16
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_office_dotnet_gac_dll_load.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\excel.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\mspub.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\onenote.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\onenoteim.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\outlook.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\powerpnt.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\winword.exe") and FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\assembly\\GAC_MSIL"
